L091 portable publication plan
=============================

Mathematical authority
----------------------

The root review ``principal_root_review/manifest.json`` has SHA-256
``3ac722a21723c2a712bfb0f98b3490880a86e74fbcdb0ba26f46cd62fb6b8131`` and
status ``ACCEPTED_COMPLETE_CORRECTED_L091_SOURCE_DISPOSITION``.  Its entire
closure supplies 76,543 canonical logical paths and 47,866 distinct
contents. Stage02 additionally retains seven literal installation aliases from
the author dependencies, giving 76,550 logical bindings without new content.  The author synthesis, its accepted proof chapters, source readings,
computational evidence and review records all remain exact.

The private inventory finds 37,382 exact content routes in previously
published files.  Their decoded content totals 5,611,096,482 bytes.  They are
only reuse candidates until the stage builder and distinct replay verify the
actual complete public files, encoded streams and decoded streams.  Original
source documents and installation files form 1,190 explicitly enumerated
premise objects; that list does not classify a derived proof or table as an
environmental premise.

The remaining 9,294 contents total 1,875,558,688 decoded bytes.  Streaming
measurement produces exactly 571,675,809 encoded bytes.  These figures measure
publication storage, never mathematical compression.

Reuse of the existing publication implementation
------------------------------------------------

``pack_codec.py`` and ``codec_controls.py`` are unchanged copies from
``geometry/chiral_atlases/publication_work``.  ``prior_transport_reader.py`` is
an unchanged copy of that publication's ``portable_check.py``; only its Archive
class is imported.  Its old main routine is not called.

The new stage builder uses the same content codec and 48 MiB bounded packs.  It
adds reuse of an existing stream that may occupy several segments of earlier
packs.  Each segment is bounded by an authenticated complete public file and
the stream retains its independent encoded and decoded hashes.  Empty content
needs no physical segment and does not add an unused public-file declaration.

The new checker has three responsibilities: authenticate the exact full
transport, rerun the unchanged accepted small occurrence join, and audit the
readable mathematical documents.  It restores thirty-one inputs, about 2.8 MB,
for ``ledger_check`` and ``controls``.  It does not invoke the old verifier's
main function, restore its entire input tree, or start GAP, Traces, a subgroup
census or another scientific search.  The complete occurrence and damage
outputs must equal those from the accepted root review.

Every accepted author TeX/PDF is copied verbatim.  The native input audit also
carries the bound ``local_structure_atoms_v1/counts.tex`` at the relative path
``proofs/counts.tex``, required by chapter ten.  The accepted author convenience
tree had omitted this auxiliary file; the mathematical chapter and table bytes
are unchanged.  There are twenty-eight main TeX files and thirty-seven adjacent
input occurrences.

The full volume has eleven new synthesis pages, one divider and sixty-six
unchanged mathematical chapter pages.  Its pdfpages invocation adds volume
numbers outside the imported mathematical content.  All sixty-six imported
Form streams are byte-identical to the accepted chapter page streams.  Fresh
compilation additionally checks the complete extracted text and all eleven
previously viewed synthesis rasters.  Exact copies and unchanged streams do
not imply a fresh independent rereading of every older chapter.

Resources and execution
------------------------

Root authorized the existing 4 GiB reserve.  The stage preflight requires that
reserve plus the measured payload and a 100 MiB allowance for metadata and
readable manuscripts.  Every codec write samples available space.  Metadata
and readable copies also check the reserve against their exact size before
writing.  The codec's legacy error text says 8 GiB, but the explicit numeric
argument passed to it is 4 GiB.  That unchanged diagnostic text does not weaken
the numerical guard.  Partial failures are retained and are not acceptance.

The first preflight recorded a storage hold before creating stage01.  No
payload or scientific output was produced by that attempt.  The builder may
be invoked again at the same still-absent path once the unchanged guard passes.

The portable replay requires external SHA-256 pins for the immutable stage
manifest and transport.  In addition to the accepted ten mathematical damage
controls, it executes the unchanged codec tests, fifteen metadata/boundary
rejections, two actual CLI gate rejections and ordinary-Python guards.

Root owns distinct operational review, public installation, registration,
commit and push.  This private preparation changes no catalogue counts and
claims no new conjecture, Lean theorem or mathematical compression factor.

Observed publication replay
---------------------------

Stage01 was preserved after its first replay found the seven literal author
installation aliases absent from the canonical root paths. Five aliases refer
to exact environment premises and two to software already carried as public
payload. Stage02 adds only these logical bindings and the corresponding
admission checks. It reuses all twelve immutable packs without another codec
run. Its full author replay passed in 44.03 seconds, including all payload
identities, the unchanged occurrence join, native rebuilds and controls.
The complete stage is 625,229,223 bytes. No public registration has occurred.
